.TH EXTRACT 1 "August 2026" "pack-extract 1.5.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
extract \- automatically extract compressed archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B extract
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.br
.B extract
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B extract
.RB [ \-C
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-f | \-n | \-i ]
.I archive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B extract
opens
.I archive
with
.BR libarchive (3)
(all supported formats and filters) and writes members into the current
directory (or into
.I dir
when
.B \-C
is given). After a successful extraction it prints a sorted list of
extracted paths.
.PP
Absolute member paths and path components equal to
.B ..
are rejected in software. Extraction also enables libarchive's
.BR ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_SECURE_SYMLINKS ,
.BR ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_SECURE_NODOTDOT ,
and
.B ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_SECURE_NOABSOLUTEPATHS
options so a symlink on disk cannot redirect writes outside the extract
tree.
.PP
Default overwrite policy: if a member path already exists,
.B extract
asks whether to overwrite
.RB ( y / N )
when stdin and stdout are a tty; otherwise a conflict aborts with an error.
Answer
.B n
(or Enter) to skip that member.
.B Ctrl+C
cancels the whole extraction.
Existing directories that match a directory member are merged without prompting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " dir\fR, \fB\-\-directory " dir
Change to
.I dir
before extracting. A relative
.I archive
path is resolved before the directory change.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Overwrite existing files without prompting.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-no\-clobber
Never overwrite; skip members whose paths already exist.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Always prompt before overwrite (requires a tty; non-tty conflicts still abort).
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.PP
Only one of
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-n ,
or
.B \-i
may be specified.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
Anything
.B libarchive
can read with
.B archive_read_support_format_all
and
.B archive_read_support_filter_all
on the build host, typically including tar (with gzip, xz, bzip2, zstd,
lz4, lzip, lzop, brotli when available), zip, 7z, cpio, and common
single-file compression streams.
.PP
Exact coverage depends on how
.B libarchive
was built (optional codecs).
.SH EXAMPLES
Extract a gzip-compressed tarball:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ extract backup.tar.gz
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract into a directory, forcing overwrite:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ extract \-C /tmp/out \-f project.zip
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract without clobbering existing files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ extract \-n data.7z
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful extraction.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (file not found, unsafe path, secure-symlink refusal,
unsupported or corrupt archive, I/O failure).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B extract
links against
.BR libarchive (3).
Build requires the libarchive development package and
.BR pkg-config (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pack (1),
.BR libarchive (3)
